From: Konstantin Pereiaslov <perk11.info>
Subject: [PATCH] tcg/wasm64: TCG backend emitting wasm — chaining + per-batch modules

Phases 1, 2a and 2 of doc/wasm-tcg-backend-plan.md.  One wasm module
per TB, compiled lazily at first execution through the browser
WebAssembly API; regs as typed wasm locals; qemu_ld/st via the *_mmu
helpers; single `loop` + region-`if` label scheme; exits by return code
to the C dispatcher (tcg_qemu_tb_exec), goto_ptr via a handoff slot.

Chaining (2a): goto_tb reads tb->jmp_target_addr[n] (maintained by qemu
core, TCI-style) at runtime and tail-calls the target TB through a
shared funcref table (return_call_indirect); unlinked slots fall through
to the exit code, which lets cpu_exec's tb_add_jump link the pair.  TB
prologues call an imported w64_tb_account(icount) at every entry
(dispatcher or chain target) so icount2 + the lockstep fold stay
per-TB-entry exact while chained; a chain_stop brake unwinds chains at
the lockstep budget; a target-fidx term keeps future batch eviction
(LRU) sound.

Batching (2): every translated TB joins an open batch while still
executing immediately through a single-member temp module.  Call sites
emit fixed-width 2-byte funcidx LEBs; every N TBs (default 128,
W64_BATCH_N env, W64_NOBATCH=1 disables) one batch module is assembled —
union type/import tables deduped across members, call indices rewritten
in place, one active element segment per member registering its function
into the shared chain table at its tidx, one addFunction'd
run(env, sp, tp, tidx) thunk — and instantiated synchronously.  Members'
descriptors flip to the thunk (desc+4 = 0x80000000|batch id), the temp
modules are removeFunction'd and become garbage.  tb_flush drops the
batch thunks, open-batch temps and chain-table entries and recycles the
tidx space.  Steady state holds ~live_TBs/128 instances instead of one
per TB.

Two emscripten -O3 optimizer artifacts worked around (documented in
doc/wasm-tcg-backend-progress.md): the helper-return typecode inlining
bug (inline literal switch) and a filler miscompile where a reassigned
`content` landed as 255 when 127 was computed (custom-section LEB) —
bytes are now precomputed into locals.

Gates: tcg-isa op-suite 1156/1156; lockstep vs native JIT 20M/250M/700M
insn windows clean (internal-SRAM digest HARD-identical); with batching
the full 2.5e9 one-insn-per-tb gate passes (298 SRAM digests + serial
identical, renderer RSS flat ~1.9GB — previously renderer OOM at 761M
insns under ~800k live per-TB modules).  S75 v=2..7 window 38.1s,
TCI reference 22.0s.
